From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 14:06:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(connection): allow confirmed blacklisted server joins

Keep ViaBedrock's server-ban warning visible and add an explicit Join
anyway action for StackAnvil users. Show the warning before connection
setup, including HTTP NetherNet targets, and retain Cancel as a normal
return to the previous screen.

Scope confirmation to the selected ServerAddress during synchronous
ConnectScreen setup, then carry it on that screen's own worker and
UserConnection. Never change disable-server-blacklist globally or retain
approval for a reconnect, another address, or another thread. Keep the
core blacklist check active for all connections without explicit consent.

This is a StackAnvil-only opt-in, not a claim that listed servers now
support translated clients. The upstream blacklist and its ban-risk
warning remain authoritative. Unit tests cover attempt identity, thread
isolation, failure cleanup, and nested setup.
